   {
    "name": "ambulance_agreement.txt",
    "text": "Sentinel Ambulance Service\nBookings Office\n\n13 March 2027\n\nDear Joan Kowalczyk,\n\nThank you for your booking and payment. This letter is your agreement with us for ambulance cover at the Lakeshore Sunset Run 10K on 12 June 2027. One ambulance and two paramedics will be on site at the old mill car park, in place by 08:00, and will stay until the race has finished. Booking reference EV-43838.\n\nOur crew leader will find your race director when they arrive.\n\nKind regards,\nRuth Abernathy\nBookings Manager\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "crowd_plan.txt",
    "text": "Looking after people on the day: Lakeshore Sunset Run 10K, Saturday 12 June 2027\n\nJoan Kowalczyk, Event Secretary, Lakeshore Striders\n\nWe expect about 1400 people altogether, including 1400 runners. Few people come just to watch.\n\nWhere people will watch\nPeople always find a good spot! Most folks gather near the start and finish and others cheer from their own front doors along the way, which the runners love. We'll have a coffee stall near the finish, and it's a nice atmosphere for families.\n\nHow we start the race\nEverybody lines up together at the start just before 09:30. We have a warm-up with music and a countdown from the crowd, then off they go. It really is a highlight of the day and people look forward to it.\n\nWho's helping\nWe've got 28 stewards in tabards, about one for every 50 people, with 3 supervisors in charge of sections. Each has a set position on a rota, and all come to a briefing an hour before the start.\n\nGetting everyone away\nRunners walk through a one-way funnel after the line, out to the recovery area, and leave by the north gate. Spectators have two marked ways out, and a steward stands at each to keep it clear. We reckon the whole place empties in 25 minutes.\n\nWho's in charge\nJoan Kowalczyk runs the event from the control point with a radio to every supervisor. They can hold a wave, stop the race, or make an announcement over the speakers to move people along. Supervisors call it in if a pen or viewing spot looks to be getting too full.\n\nFamilies are welcome, and there is usually a friendly atmosphere at the finish. Local shops have been supportive, and some stay open for the day. The prize-giving takes place at the end, and there is often a queue for tea.\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "insurance.txt",
    "text": "CERTIFICATE OF LIABILITY INSURANCE\nCertificate no. PH-55059\nIssued: March 13, 2027\n\nINSURER: Harbourline Insurance Company\nPOLICY NUMBER: PL-649287\n\nNAMED INSURED: Lakeshore Striders\nDESCRIPTION OF OPERATIONS: Public liability for a foot race, the Lakeshore Sunset Run 10K\nVENUE: Ferry Park, Port Halden\n\nPOLICY PERIOD\nEffective: January 1, 2027\nExpiry: December 31, 2027\n\nLIMIT OF LIABILITY: $1,000,000 each occurrence\n\nThis certificate is issued for information only and confers no rights upon the holder beyond those of the policy.\n\nCertificate holder: City of Port Halden, Events Office\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "medical_plan.txt",
    "text": "Lakeshore Sunset Run 10K - medical notes\nSaturday 12 June 2027 / gun 09:30 / 1400 runners / 10K\ncontact Joan Kowalczyk 555-0115\nOn-site ambulance cover is set out in the attached paperwork from Sentinel Ambulance Service.\n\nFIRST AID\ncommittee members w/ work first aid certs. kit at HQ tent + kit in lead car\n\npast yrs: last runner well inside limit, only blisters + one twisted ankle. some members have work first aid certs, general helping\n\nWEATHER / WATER\npre-race email tells runners dress for weather + drink plenty. will watch forecast\n\nHOSPITAL\nHarbourside Medical Centre, 10km from finish. pickup point the old mill car park, route walked w/ first aiders. ED told date + numbers\n\nCOMMS\nteam phones. number list circulated week before. signal ok usually\n\nLEAD\nOwen Cartwright, registered paramedic, on site from -1hr til last runner in. can withdraw any runner\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "race_plan.txt",
    "text": "Lakeshore Sunset Run 10K - race notes\nLakeshore Striders / contact Joan Kowalczyk 555-0115\nSaturday 12 June 2027, gun 09:30, course closes 11:30\n10K (10k), approx 1400 entered\n\nROUTE\nRiverside Path then Pier Promenade. no roads, no closures. finish the pavilion\n\nWIDTHS\nRiverside Path 3m, rail one side wall other. Pier Promenade 3m. 2-3 abreast max. start strung along path\n\nOTHER\nnumbers from the old mill car park 1hr before. chip timing. water on course. results online same day\n"
   }
  ],
  "cover_letter": "Hello,\n\nI am writing on behalf of our organisation about this year's race.\n\nHere is our application for the Lakeshore Sunset Run 10K, Saturday 12 June 2027. 1400 runners, 10K, off at 09:30, around Ferry Park. I've attached ambulance_agreement.txt, crowd_plan.txt, insurance.txt, medical_plan.txt, race_plan.txt.\n\nPlease let me know if you need anything else.\n\nThanks,\nJoan\n\nJoan Kowalczyk, Lakeshore Striders\n555-0115\n",
